### S04: As an organizer, I want to publish and unpublish an event, so that I control when it goes public

**Acceptance Criteria**

1. Given an organizer has created an event and added at least one ticket tier, when the organizer publishes the event, then the event's status changes from `draft` to `published`, and it becomes visible in the public event list.

2. Given an event is currently published, when the organizer unpublishes it, then its status changes from `published` to `draft`, and it is no longer visible in the public event list.

3. Given an organizer has created an event but has not added any ticket tiers, when the organizer tries to publish it, then the system returns an `INVALID_STATE` error, and the event remains a draft.